/-!
# Twisting a dualizing module by the sheaf of an effective Cartier divisor

Let `X` be a locally Noetherian scheme, `D ⊆ X` an effective Cartier divisor and `ω` a
quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module whose complex `ω[n]` is a dualizing complex on `X` in the sense of
[Stacks, Tag 0A87]. This file proves that the twist `𝒪_X(D) ⊗_{𝒪_X} ω`, placed in degree zero,
is again a dualizing complex on `X`.

The argument is affine-local. Being a dualizing complex is a condition at one affine open
through every point ([Stacks, Tag 0A86]), and an effective Cartier divisor is cut out, on an
affine open around any given point, by a single nonzerodivisor ([Stacks, Tag 01WR]). Over such
an open the ideal sheaf `ℐ_D` is trivial, hence so is the invertible sheaf `𝒪_X(D) = ℐ_D^∨`
([Stacks, Tag 01WX]) — the evaluation pairing `𝒪_X(D) ⊗ ℐ_D ≅ 𝒪_X` restricts to a
trivialization of `𝒪_X(D)` once `ℐ_D` is trivialized — and therefore the restriction of the
twist to that open is the restriction of `ω`. The ring-level hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 0A7B]
at that open is then the one carried by `ω` itself.

The degree collapses to zero because the ring-level statement extracted from `ω[n]` over an
affine open is already normalized to degree zero; see
`Stacks.Duality.isDualizingComplex_single_specModule`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Divisors.restrictNegativeTwistIsoUnit` — the trivialization of the ideal sheaf `ℐ_D`
  over an affine open on which the ideal is generated by a nonzerodivisor, read in the
  open-subspace model of modules rather than the slice-site model.
* `Stacks.Divisors.restrictDivisorSheafIsoUnit` — the resulting trivialization of `𝒪_X(D)`.
* `Stacks.Divisors.restrictDivisorSheafTensorIso` and
  `Stacks.Divisors.restrictFunctorDivisorSheafTensorIso` — the identification
  `(𝒪_X(D) ⊗ ω)|_U ≅ ω|_U` over such an open, in the two models of restriction.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Duality.isDualizingComplex_single_divisorSheaf_tensor` — if `ω[n]` is a dualizing
  complex then so is `(𝒪_X(D) ⊗_{𝒪_X} ω)[0]`.

## Implementation notes

The two models of restriction of sheaves of modules to an open both occur. The trivialization of
the ideal sheaf is available in the slice-site model, as
`Stacks.Divisors.idealSheafOverIsoUnit`, while the compatibility of restriction with the tensor
product, `Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorPower.restrictTensorSheafIso`, is stated for the
open-subspace restriction `Stacks.Cohomology.HigherDirectImage.moduleRestriction`, and
`Stacks.Duality.HasDualizingModelOn` is phrased with Mathlib's
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor` along `U.ι`. The first passage is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.overToRestricted` and the second is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.restrictModulesIsoRestrictFunctor`; everything in between is
assembled by composing isomorphisms, since the categories `X.Modules` and
`SheafOfModules (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace)` are equal but not syntactically so, and
rewriting across morphism equations between them is not type-correct at `rewrite`'s
transparency.

The restriction of `SheafOfModules.unit` is `SheafOfModules.unit` on the nose, which is why no
comparison for the unit object appears below.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A86](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A86)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A87](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A87)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B4R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B4R)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE
open Stacks.Cohomology.HigherDirectImage
open Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorPower (ringedSpaceIsSheaf)

universe u w

attribute [local instance 10000] HasDerivedCategory.standard

namespace Stacks.Divisors

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (D : X.IdealSheafData)

/-- **The ideal sheaf of a divisor is trivial over an affine open where it is generated by a
nonzerodivisor**, in the open-subspace model of modules on the open.

`Stacks.Divisors.idealSheafOverIsoUnit` is this trivialization in the slice-site model, over the
site of opens contained in `U`; `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.overToRestricted` is the
equivalence between the two models, and it carries one to the other with no further data. -/
def restrictNegativeTwistIsoUnit {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {f : Γ(X, U)}
    (hf : IsRegular f) (hgen : D.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩ = Ideal.span {f}) :
    (moduleRestriction X.toRingedSpace U).obj (negativeTwist' D) ≅
      SheafOfModules.unit (structureSheafRing (restrictToOpen X.toRingedSpace U)) :=
  (AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.overToRestricted X.toRingedSpace U).mapIso
    (idealSheafOverIsoUnit D hU hf hgen (mem_ker_app_of_ideal_eq_span D hU hgen))

/-- **The invertible sheaf `𝒪_X(D)` of an effective Cartier divisor is trivial over an affine
open where the ideal is generated by a nonzerodivisor.**

This is the evaluation pairing `𝒪_X(D) ⊗_{𝒪_X} ℐ_D ≅ 𝒪_X` of [Stacks, Tag 01WX] restricted to
`U`: the tensor product commutes with restriction, the second factor becomes the unit by
`Stacks.Divisors.restrictNegativeTwistIsoUnit`, and tensoring with the unit on the right is the
identity. -/
def restrictDivisorSheafIsoUnit [IsEffectiveCartierDivisor D] {U : X.Opens}
    (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {f : Γ(X, U)} (hf : IsRegular f)
    (hgen : D.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩ = Ideal.span {f}) :
    (moduleRestriction X.toRingedSpace U).obj (divisorSheaf D) ≅
      SheafOfModules.unit (structureSheafRing (restrictToOpen X.toRingedSpace U)) :=
  haveI := isTensorInvertible_negativeTwist D
  (Stacks.SheafOfModules.tensorLeftFunctorObjUnitIso
        (restrictToOpen X.toRingedSpace U).presheaf
        (ringedSpaceIsSheaf (restrictToOpen X.toRingedSpace U))
        ((moduleRestriction X.toRingedSpace U).obj (divisorSheaf D))).symm ≪≫
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorPower.tensorSheafMapIso _ _ (Iso.refl _)
      (restrictNegativeTwistIsoUnit D hU hf hgen).symm ≪≫
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorPower.restrictTensorSheafIso X.toRingedSpace U
      (divisorSheaf D) (negativeTwist' D)).symm ≪≫
    (moduleRestriction X.toRingedSpace U).mapIso
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Scheme.evaluationIso X (negativeTwist' D))

/-- **The twist by `𝒪_X(D)` is invisible over an affine open where the ideal of `D` is generated
by a nonzerodivisor**, in the open-subspace model of modules on the open: the restriction of
`𝒪_X(D) ⊗_{𝒪_X} ω` is the restriction of `ω`.

The tensor product commutes with restriction, the first factor becomes the unit by
`Stacks.Divisors.restrictDivisorSheafIsoUnit`, and the braiding moves it to the right, where
tensoring with the unit is the identity. -/
def restrictDivisorSheafTensorIso [IsEffectiveCartierDivisor D] (ω : X.Modules)
    {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {f : Γ(X, U)} (hf : IsRegular f)
    (hgen : D.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩ = Ideal.span {f}) :
    (moduleRestriction X.toRingedSpace U).obj
        (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor
            (Stacks.SheafOfModules.ringedSite X.sheaf).O).obj (divisorSheaf D)).obj ω) ≅
      (moduleRestriction X.toRingedSpace U).obj ω :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorPower.restrictTensorSheafIso X.toRingedSpace U
      (divisorSheaf D) ω ≪≫
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorPower.tensorSheafMapIso _ _
      (restrictDivisorSheafIsoUnit D hU hf hgen) (Iso.refl _) ≪≫
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.tensorSheafBraiding _ _ _ _ ≪≫
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.tensorLeftFunctorObjUnitIso _ _ _

/-- **The twist by `𝒪_X(D)` is invisible over an affine open where the ideal of `D` is generated
by a nonzerodivisor**, in Mathlib's model of restriction along the open immersion `U.ι`.

This is `Stacks.Divisors.restrictDivisorSheafTensorIso` conjugated by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.restrictModulesIsoRestrictFunctor`, the identification of the
open-subspace restriction with restriction along `U.ι`. It is the shape that
`Stacks.Duality.HasDualizingModelOn` consumes. -/
def restrictFunctorDivisorSheafTensorIso [IsEffectiveCartierDivisor D] (ω : X.Modules)
    {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {f : Γ(X, U)} (hf : IsRegular f)
    (hgen : D.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩ = Ideal.span {f}) :
    (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor U.ι).obj
        (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor
            (Stacks.SheafOfModules.ringedSite X.sheaf).O).obj (divisorSheaf D)).obj ω) ≅
      (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor U.ι).obj ω :=
  ((AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.restrictModulesIsoRestrictFunctor X U).app _).symm ≪≫
    restrictDivisorSheafTensorIso D ω hU hf hgen ≪≫
    (AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.restrictModulesIsoRestrictFunctor X U).app ω

end Stacks.Divisors

namespace Stacks.Duality

/-- **Twisting a dualizing module by the invertible sheaf of an effective Cartier divisor again
gives a dualizing complex.** If `ω` is a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module on a locally Noetherian
scheme `X` whose complex `ω[n]` is a dualizing complex ([Stacks, Tag 0A87]), and `D ⊆ X` is an
effective Cartier divisor, then `(𝒪_X(D) ⊗_{𝒪_X} ω)[0]` is a dualizing complex on `X`.

Around every point there is an affine open `U` on which the ideal of `D` is generated by a
nonzerodivisor ([Stacks, Tag 01WR]); over `U` the twist is invisible, by
`Stacks.Divisors.restrictFunctorDivisorSheafTensorIso`, so the `Γ(X, U)`-module of sections of
`ω` presents the restriction of the twist, and it is a dualizing complex over `Γ(X, U)` because
`ω[n]` is dualizing on `X`. The passage from one affine open through every point to the global
statement is [Stacks, Tag 0A86]. -/
theorem isDualizingComplex_single_divisorSheaf_tensor
    {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (D : X.IdealSheafData)
    [Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor D] (ω : X.Modules) [ω.IsQuasicoherent] (n : ℤ)
    (hω : Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingComplex
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules n).obj ω)) :
    Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingComplex
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules 0).obj
        (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor
            (Stacks.SheafOfModules.ringedSite X.sheaf).O).obj
          (Stacks.Divisors.divisorSheaf D)).obj ω)) := by
  refine isDualizingComplex_single_of_forall_exists_module_iso _ 0 fun x => ?_
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hxU, f, hf, hgen⟩ :=
    Stacks.Divisors.exists_affineOpen_ideal_eq_span_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor D
      inferInstance x
  exact ⟨U, hU, hxU, specModule ω hU,
    Stacks.Divisors.restrictFunctorDivisorSheafTensorIso D ω hU hf hgen ≪≫
      restrictSpecTildeModuleIso ω hU,
    isDualizingComplex_single_specModule ω n hω U hU⟩

end Stacks.Duality

end
